in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @cascade
in @labeled
in @facet/gleam
in @facet/beam

# @cascade/code/gleam/beam — the Gleam → BEAM bytecode cascade species.
#
# Path naming: per Alex 2026-06-23 directive — cascade species shards
# group by `@cascade/code/<source>/<target>`. Source language (Gleam)
# groups together; targets (beam here; js in the sibling shard
# shards/cascade/code/gleam/js.mirror) are leaves. This is the
# A4 dual-target species pair instance: ONE source, TWO targets,
# TWO shards under one source directory.
#
# Per recognition #95 candidate (@cascade as loss-lens substrate;
# Mara canonical ce4874b 2026-06-23): each cascade species shard
# discharges the per-grammar measurement of information loss in
# compilation from a typed source grammar to a mainstream target.
#
# This species: source_grammar = @facet/gleam, target_grammar =
# @facet/beam (shards/code/beam.mirror; landed 2026-06-19 by Reed).
# The Gleam→BEAM cascade IS GLEAM'S NATIVE TARGET; the BEAM-side
# runtime preserves the dimensions JS cannot: preemptive
# concurrency, supervision trees, hot code upgrade, the OTP
# behaviour family. The dual-target asymmetry is the load-bearing
# substrate observation: same source, different target, different
# loss profile.
#
# === The cascade shape (Gleam→BEAM) ===
#
# Source (Gleam admits):
# - sound static typing (ADTs, generics, opaque types)
# - structural exhaustiveness (the `case` statement)
# - immutability by default
# - explicit error handling (Result, Option)
# - module-level encapsulation
# - actor-model concurrency (via stdlib's gleam_otp wrapping
#   Erlang's gen_server / supervisor primitives)
#
# Target (BEAM preserves):
# - typed atom tags for ADT constructors (preserved via Erlang's
#   atom + tuple discipline; tag is first element of tuple)
# - pattern matching (BEAM's match/2 instruction; preserves
#   exhaustiveness at runtime via the `function_clause` error
#   when no clause matches)
# - immutability (BEAM enforces by language)
# - preemptive scheduling (BEAM scheduler; each process is
#   independently scheduled per @facet/beam's discipline)
# - supervision tree (gen_supervisor; restart strategies;
#   per @facet/beam.swap_module + @facet/beam.supervise actions)
# - hot code upgrade (BEAM's two-version-coexistence per
#   @facet/beam.code_change_msg + @facet/beam.code_change action)
# - the @magic/contract preservation across hot swaps (per
#   @facet/beam's composition with @magic per recognition #80)
#
# Loss surfaces at: static type erasure (the type system itself
# vanishes at runtime; BEAM is dynamically typed; the
# constructor-tag-as-atom IS the preserved discrimination but the
# type system is not present); generic erasure (parametric
# polymorphism collapses to BEAM's dynamic dispatch); opaque-type
# erasure (the encapsulation guarantee is compile-time-only).
#
# CRITICAL ASYMMETRY (with the js.mirror sibling): BEAM PRESERVES
# the concurrency dimension. The actor-model concurrency that
# Gleam→JS erases is NATIVELY preserved here. The loss profile of
# Gleam→BEAM is substrate-architecturally SHALLOWER than the loss
# profile of Gleam→JS; the difference is exactly the BEAM-
# preserved dimensions (concurrency, supervision, hot upgrade).
#
# The loss_lens<@facet/gleam, @facet/beam> measures these gaps
# against the Gleam compiler's emitted type info + the BEAM grammar
# specification.
#
# === Why Gleam → BEAM as the dual-target sibling ===
#
# Per Mara's survey §2.7 (Gleam dossier in
# docs/research/2026-06-23-typed-alternatives-cascade-survey.md):
# Gleam compiles to TWO mainstream targets from one source —
# `gleam build --target javascript` emits JS; `gleam build
# --target erlang` emits BEAM bytecode. The dual-target shape IS
# THE substrate-pull-correct test of the @cascade family-root's
# parametric form: one source carrier, two target species, the
# loss profiles substrate-architecturally distinct.
#
# This shard (beam.mirror) lands the BEAM arm of the dual-target
# pair. The sibling shard (js.mirror at shards/cascade/code/gleam/
# js.mirror) lands the JS arm. Both share gleam_source as their
# carrier; both share the gleam_well_typed source-side bilateral;
# both specialize the same family-root actions; the loss signatures
# DIFFER because BEAM preserves substrate dimensions JS erases.
#
# The composed cascade<gleam, {js, beam}> at species altitude is
# NOT a third shard; it IS the composition-by-co-presence of the
# two species shards (js.mirror + beam.mirror) under @cascade/code/
# gleam/. The dual-target shape per Mara survey §2.7 validates the
# parametric form of the family-root.
#
# === First applied consumer ===
#
# Forward-promised: any BEAM-side runtime consumer of Gleam-
# authored services. The natural production-shape candidates:
#   /Users/reed/body/ (Reed's BEAM body; Elixir + Erlang). Future
#                     Gleam-authored services could co-deploy via
#                     this cascade species.
#   gleam_otp ecosystem consumers (any Gleam server that needs
#                                   supervision-tree + hot upgrade
#                                   discipline; cascades through
#                                   this species into BEAM).
#
# Honest hedge: spectral.engineer's CURRENT content cascade is
# Gleam→JS (via the js.mirror sibling), NOT Gleam→BEAM. This shard
# does not name a load-bearing live consumer in the spectral.
# engineer site; it lands the substrate-decl for the dual-target
# shape and the BEAM-deployment-future. The substrate-pull-correct
# move is to LAND the species now (so the dual-target parametric
# form is closed at substrate-decl altitude) and let production
# consumers attach when they need the BEAM-side discipline.
#
# === Recognition ancestry ===
#
# - Recognition #95 (@cascade candidate; Mara canonical ce4874b):
#   this species IS the FIFTH species discharge of the family-root
#   (after purescript/js A3, rust/wasm A5, gleam/js sibling, and
#   THIS shard).
# - Recognition #93 H4 RESOLVED (labeled<> functor at
#   shards/labeled.mirror): beam_artifact uses labeled<> instance.
# - Recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert space): the dual-
#   target case directly evidences that the loss measurement IS a
#   dimension-projection per target — same source, two projections,
#   each preserving a different basis of the source's
#   dimensionality. The BEAM-target preserves more basis vectors
#   than the JS-target; the loss is correspondingly smaller.
# - Recognition #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics): the Gleam↔
#   BEAM boundary IS the @io altitude this species operationalizes;
#   the boundary is where Gleam's static types meet BEAM's
#   dynamic-runtime invariants. The substrate-pull-correct boundary
#   discharge composes with @facet/beam's @magic-derived discipline
#   (recognition #80) for runtime-altitude correctness.
# - Recognition #80 (@magic family; @facet/beam composes with):
#   the BEAM target's hot-upgrade and supervision discipline
#   composes through this species; a Gleam-authored gen_server
#   compiled to BEAM inherits the @magic/contract preservation
#   discipline that @facet/beam declares.
# - Recognition #59 (kintsugi loop altitude-portable): @kintsugi
#   heals the loss this species measures, including at the BEAM
#   runtime-upgrade altitude where hot swaps are the operational
#   form of the kintsugi loop.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Gleam language                 Louis Pilfold 2018-present; the
#                                  source grammar this species
#                                  measures.
#   Gleam Erlang backend           Pilfold + contributors
#                                  2018-present; the original
#                                  compiler subsystem (BEAM was
#                                  Gleam's first target before JS).
#   gleam_otp                      the Gleam wrapper around OTP
#                                  behaviours; the actor-model
#                                  surface this species discharges
#                                  to BEAM at.
#   Erlang/OTP                     Armstrong, Virding, Wikström,
#                                  Williams 1996-2003; the runtime
#                                  this species's target preserves
#                                  semantics of.
#   BEAM VM                        the Erlang virtual machine;
#                                  per @facet/beam's substrate-decl
#                                  (shards/code/beam.mirror).
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/recognitions/recognition-95-cascade-as-
#               loss-lens-substrate-decl.md (Mara canonical;
#               Seam DEFENSIVE pending Reed consolidation);
#               docs/research/2026-06-23-typed-alternatives-cascade-
#               survey.md §2.7 (the Gleam dossier; dual-target
#               shape named as substrate-pull-correct test of the
#               parametric form).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]],
#                      [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]]
#                      (loss is @epistemologic/properties composite,
#                      not Shannon, not invented).
# Related shards: shards/cascade.mirror (the family-root this
#                 specializes); shards/labeled.mirror (the functor
#                 primitive beam_artifact instance rests on);
#                 shards/code/gleam.mirror (source grammar);
#                 shards/code/beam.mirror (target grammar; composes
#                 with @magic per recognition #80);
#                 shards/cascade/code/gleam/js.mirror (the sibling
#                 dual-target species; same source, different target);
#                 shards/cascade/code/rust/wasm.mirror (pattern
#                 reference for the rustc-as-source-toolchain shape).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/cascade/code/gleam/beam.mirror` declares
# `@cascade/code/gleam/beam` per
# `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.
#
# === Honest hedges ===
#
# 1. OTP version pinning. The BEAM target's runtime invariants
#    evolve with the OTP release line (OTP 27 / OTP 28 / OTP 29).
#    Hot-code-upgrade semantics, supervisor restart strategies,
#    and the gen_server callback surface have all evolved across
#    OTP versions in compatible-but-distinguishable ways. The
#    substrate-decl assumes 2026's stable OTP 28+ shape; if the
#    OTP release breaks compatibility at runtime, bundle_beam's
#    body discharges differently but the substrate-decl stays
#    stable. The beam_consumable bilateral discharges against the
#    source's declared target OTP version at realisation boundary.
#
# 2. gleam_stdlib + gleam_otp version pinning. Gleam's stdlib +
#    OTP wrapping evolve; the emitted .beam bytecode shape can
#    change across major versions. Same hedge shape as js.mirror's
#    hedge 2; bundle_beam discharges per-version.
#
# 3. FFI escape hatch. Gleam admits FFI to native Erlang via the
#    `@external` decorator with target=erlang; FFI code is OUTSIDE
#    the typing discipline (the type signature is declared on the
#    Gleam side, the body lives in raw Erlang). The same hedge as
#    js.mirror's hedge 3; the bilateral gleam_well_typed carries
#    the Narcissus-warned pole for FFI-present programs.
#
# 4. BEAM-side substrate composition forward-promised. The composed
#    cascade well-formedness COULD declare requires @facet/beam
#    bilaterals (e.g., supervision-tree-coherent, contract-
#    preserved-across-swap) for BEAM-side runtime correctness;
#    those bilaterals don't yet exist at @facet/beam altitude
#    (per @facet/beam's own honest hedges about mechanical-glue
#    forward-promises with @magic). This shard's composed bilateral
#    stays at the cascade altitude (source typed + target
#    consumable + loss well-defined) and does NOT pre-empt the
#    BEAM-runtime bilaterals. When @magic/audit + @magic/contract
#    discharge their bilaterals, a future @cascade/code/gleam/beam
#    extension could LIFT the cascade-well-formed bilateral with
#    additional BEAM-runtime requires clauses. Today: do not
#    pre-empt.
#
# === Dual-target composition note ===
#
# (See js.mirror for the primary dual-target framing.) This shard
# is the BEAM arm. The composed cascade<gleam, {js, beam}> at
# species altitude is the composition-by-co-presence of js.mirror
# + beam.mirror under @cascade/code/gleam/. The substrate-decl
# assumes the survey-§2.7-noted invariant that the SAME
# gleam_source compiles to BOTH targets via different target flags;
# the asymmetric loss profiles are the substrate-architectural
# evidence that the family-root's parametric form is honest.

source @arxiv/programming-languages/gleam-language-tour
source @arxiv/distributed/otp-behaviours

prism @cascade/code/gleam/beam {
  focus cascade
  project cascade
  split cascade
  shift cascade
  settle cascade
}

# === gleam_source carrier ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.typed_source for source_grammar=gleam.
# References a Gleam project (gleam.toml + src/*.gleam) as the unit
# of cascade.
#
# SHARED with the sibling shard (js.mirror): the same gleam_source
# IS the input for both species. This sharing is the load-bearing
# evidence that the family-root's parametric form is honest — one
# source carrier, two target species, no duplication. The carrier
# is intentionally re-declared in both species shards; the bytes-
# equal nature of the type declaration IS the substrate's witness
# that the two species share their source.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the source-tree content hash.
type gleam_source = ref

# === gleam_module carrier ===
#
# The output of `gleam build --target erlang`. Compiled Erlang
# beam bytecode + .erl source intermediate + the emitted
# gleam_stdlib + gleam_otp runtime support that bridges Gleam's
# typed surface to BEAM's dynamic-runtime invariants. The .beam
# bytecode IS the substrate-architectural deliverable;
# measure_gleam_beam reads the gleam-emitted type info + the .beam
# files to discharge the substrate-typed gap calculation.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type gleam_module = ref

# === beam_metadata carrier ===
#
# Structured carrier for BEAM bundling shape (application name,
# OTP version target, supervisor entrypoint module, gleam_stdlib
# version, gleam_otp version, release shape). Per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: structured, not stringly. The carrier
# names load-bearing fields without fixing one release shape (per
# hedges 1+2: OTP version and stdlib version are fields).
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type beam_metadata = ref

# === beam_artifact carrier ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING NEW CARRIER. The @labeled<> instance per
# recognition #93 H4. A beam_artifact IS a gleam_module annotated
# with beam_metadata via the labeled functor.
#
# Substrate-architecturally load-bearing: the gleam_module's typed
# identity is preserved (via labeled's parametricity per Wadler
# 1989 / Reynolds 1983) while the beam_metadata dimension is added.
# unlabel(artifact) returns the module; label_of(artifact) returns
# the metadata. The cascade preserves typed source identity AND adds
# release/bundling dimension AT ONE CARRIER altitude.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the (module, metadata) pair
# (inherited from @labeled).
type beam_artifact = labeled(gleam_module, beam_metadata)

# === compile_gleam_beam action ===
#
# Specialization of @cascade.compile for this cascade. Takes a
# gleam_source and perturbation; returns the gleam_module via
# `gleam build --target erlang`.
#
# Per recognition #51 (Hilbert space dimension growth): compile_
# gleam_beam IS a DIMENSION PROJECTION. Gleam admits typed-feature
# dimensions (ADTs, generics, exhaustiveness, opaque types); the
# BEAM runtime preserves constructor-tag-as-atom dispatch + match-
# instruction discrimination + immutability + preemptive
# concurrency + supervision-tree discipline. Lossy by construction
# at the type-system altitude; loss-PRESERVING at the runtime-
# discipline altitude (in contrast to the JS target).
#
# requires gleam_well_typed(source, p): the substrate forecloses
# compilation against type errors. The Gleam compiler runs the
# typing discipline; the bilateral verdict reflects what it reports.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
compile_gleam_beam(source: gleam_source, p: perturbation) -> gleam_module
requires gleam_well_typed(source, p)
{ \ }

# === bundle_beam action ===
#
# Wraps a gleam_module + beam_metadata into a beam_artifact via
# @labeled.label construction. The typed module gets the
# release/bundling dimension added without losing the underlying
# module identity.
#
# Per hedges 1+2: body discharges per-OTP-version + per-stdlib-
# version (OTP 28+ default; legacy OTP fallback if the source
# pins). The substrate-decl does NOT pick versions; it declares
# the action shape.
#
# requires beam_consumable(module, metadata, p): bilateral
# commitment that the (module, metadata) pair is coherent at the
# BEAM release altitude — application name resolves, supervisor
# entrypoint is reachable, gleam_otp runtime correctly co-emitted,
# OTP version compatibility upheld.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
bundle_beam(module: gleam_module, metadata: beam_metadata, p: perturbation)
  -> beam_artifact
requires beam_consumable(module, metadata, p)
{ \ }

# === measure_gleam_beam action ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION. Specialization of @cascade.measure for
# this cascade. Returns substrate-typed measurement of information
# loss between source's typing discipline and artifact's runtime-
# preserved structure.
#
# Returns `imperfect<beam_artifact, ref, information_loss>` — the
# loss slot carries measured loss as substrate-typed data, NOT
# Shannon, NOT estimation; the composite of @epistemologic/properties
# per [[feedback-loss-from-epistemologic-properties]].
#
# The measurement IS substrate-architectural: read the source's
# typing-discipline use (ADT count, generic positions, exhaustive
# case sites, opaque-type count, FFI annotation count); read the
# artifact's runtime-preserved structure from the unlabel'd module's
# .beam bytecode + the labeled metadata; compute the dimension gap.
#
# CRITICAL ASYMMETRY (vs the js.mirror sibling): the concurrency
# dimension IS preserved on this target. The loss profile does NOT
# report concurrency-erasure as part of the composite. The loss is
# substrate-architecturally SHALLOWER than the JS cascade's loss
# on the same source; the difference IS exactly what BEAM
# preserves that JS erases (concurrency, supervision, hot upgrade).
# This asymmetry is the load-bearing observation the dual-target
# shape surfaces and the substrate-pull validation of the @cascade
# family-root's parametric form.
#
# requires gleam_beam_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p):
# bilateral that the measurement IS computable. Per hedge 3: FFI
# bounds the measurement to the typed sub-program; the bilateral
# discharges with a Narcissus-warned verdict for FFI-present
# programs.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
measure_gleam_beam(source: gleam_source, artifact: beam_artifact, p: perturbation)
  -> imperfect(beam_artifact, ref, information_loss)
requires gleam_beam_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p)
{ \ }

# === gleam_well_typed bilateral ===
#
# Source-side typing-discipline bilateral. Specializes the family-
# root's grammar_coherent at source_grammar=gleam.
#
# SHARED predicate-shape with the sibling shard (js.mirror): the
# same gleam_source must be well-typed for EITHER cascade to
# proceed; the bilateral's discharge does NOT depend on target
# choice (Gleam's typer runs identically for both target flags).
# This shard re-declares gleam_well_typed with the same shape;
# this is intentional duplication at the substrate-decl altitude —
# the property is genuinely the same property and discharges
# identically across both species.
#
# Splinter-pole: well-typed by `gleam check`; FFI (if present)
# correctly annotated at the boundary; loss measurement complete-
# capable.
# Narcissus-pole: type errors OR FFI annotations ill-formed at the
# boundary. Compilation cannot proceed.
# Narcissus-warned (per hedge 3): FFI annotations well-formed but
# FFI code outside typing discipline; measurement bounded to typed
# sub-program; FFI gap unmeasurable by this species.
gleam_well_typed(source: gleam_source, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === beam_consumable bilateral ===
#
# Target-side packaging-well-formedness bilateral. Commitment that
# the (module, metadata) pair forms a coherent BEAM release.
#
# Splinter-pole: metadata.application name resolves; supervisor
# entrypoint module is present in the artifact's .beam files;
# gleam_otp runtime correctly co-emitted; OTP version compatibility
# upheld; release shape (.app file structure) valid; consumer
# `application:start/1` would succeed.
# Narcissus-pole: release drift (missing supervisor entrypoint;
# gleam_otp version mismatch; OTP-incompatibility in emitted
# bytecode; .app file malformed).
beam_consumable(module: gleam_module, metadata: beam_metadata, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === gleam_beam_loss_well_defined bilateral ===
#
# Specializes the family-root's loss_well_defined for this cascade.
# Commitment that the substrate-typed gap calculation IS computable
# for the (source, artifact) pair.
#
# Splinter-pole: .beam bytecode readable from the artifact's
# unlabel'd module; gleam-emitted type info present; composite of
# @epistemologic/properties dischargeable; measurement bounded and
# substrate-typed.
# Narcissus-pole: bytecode malformed OR type info missing
# (compiler emission failed); substrate cannot read the typing
# residue; measurement undefined.
# Narcissus-warned: type info present but covers only the typed
# sub-program (FFI gap unmeasurable; per hedge 3).
gleam_beam_loss_well_defined(source: gleam_source, artifact: beam_artifact, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === gleam_beam_cascade_well_formed composed bilateral ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING composed bilateral. Specializes the family-root's
# cascade_well_defined for this cascade. Composes the three sub-
# predicates at this altitude.
#
# requires gleam_well_typed(source, p): source-side typing
# discipline IS coherent.
# requires beam_consumable(unlabel(artifact, p), label_of(artifact, p), p):
# target-side packaging IS well-formed; uses @labeled.unlabel +
# @labeled.label_of to extract module and metadata from the
# artifact. This labeled-projection pattern is the load-bearing
# shape Mara A3 surfaced; it makes the composed bilateral
# parametric over the labeled functor's structure rather than
# re-deriving (module, metadata) ad-hoc.
# requires gleam_beam_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p): loss
# measurement IS computable.
#
# Per hedge 4: BEAM-runtime bilaterals (supervision-tree-coherent,
# contract-preserved-across-swap) are FORWARD-PROMISED at @magic/
# audit + @magic/contract altitude per @facet/beam's own honest
# hedges; this composed bilateral does NOT pre-empt them. A future
# extension could LIFT the requires clauses when those bilaterals
# discharge.
#
# All three (current) sub-predicates must hold; substrate refuses
# cascade if source has type errors OR packaging is malformed OR
# measurement is undefined.
#
# Splinter-pole: all three discharge; substrate-typed loss returned.
# Narcissus-pole: at least one sub-predicate fails; cascade blocked.
# Narcissus-warned: all three discharge but at least one is warned
# (e.g., FFI present); cascade operates with bounded measurement;
# warning propagates to caller.
#
# Same composed-bilateral pattern as @cascade.cascade_well_defined
# (the family-root) and sibling species (purescript/js, rust/wasm,
# the gleam/js sibling). The discipline pattern is altitude-
# portable; here it instantiates at the Gleam→BEAM altitude with
# the BEAM-specific (shallower) loss profile.
gleam_beam_cascade_well_formed(source: gleam_source, artifact: beam_artifact, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires gleam_well_typed(source, p)
requires beam_consumable(unlabel(artifact, p), label_of(artifact, p), p)
requires gleam_beam_loss_well_defined(source, artifact, p)
{ \ }

out @cascade/code/gleam/beam
out gleam_source
out gleam_module
out beam_metadata
out beam_artifact
out compile_gleam_beam
out bundle_beam
out measure_gleam_beam
out gleam_well_typed
out beam_consumable
out gleam_beam_loss_well_defined
out gleam_beam_cascade_well_formed
